---
source: crates/gough-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: o.out
---
Hardware-layer orchestration for LXD clusters

Usage: gough [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  version       Print version information
  login         Authenticate against the cluster (device flow)
  logout        Remove stored credentials
  config        Read and write the local config file and contexts
  init          Bootstrap the primary node of a new cluster
  sync          Export or import cluster state
  vault         Vault operations
  primary       Primary-node lifecycle operations
  node          Manage nodes
  disk          Manage node disks
  biome         Manage biomes (workload definitions)
  cluster       Cluster-wide operations
  lxd           LXD trust-password operations
  capacity      Capacity forecasting and risk
  migration     Workload migration policy and triggers
  dr            Disaster recovery
  restore       Restore a cluster from backup (same as `dr restore`)
  audit         Audit log operations
  dev           Development helpers (simulated nodes, seed data)
  integrations  Third-party integrations
  doctor        Run diagnostic checks
  webhook       Webhook operations
  deployment    Manage deployments
  storage       Storage quotas
  completion    Generate shell completion scripts
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --version          Print version information and exit
  -o, --output <FORMAT>  Output format: table, json, yaml or jsonpath=<RFC 9535 expression> [default: table]
  -q, --quiet            Suppress all output except errors
      --no-color         Disable colored output
      --cluster <URL>    Cluster API URL (env GOUGH_CLUSTER_URL); overrides the config file
      --context <NAME>   Named context from the config file (env GOUGH_CURRENT_CONTEXT)
  -v, --verbose          Log requests and diagnostics to stderr (tokens are masked)
      --ca-file <FILE>   Extra PEM CA bundle to trust for the cluster's TLS certificate
  -h, --help             Print help

Credentials never travel on argv: set GOUGH_TOKEN in the environment (or pipe the token on
stdin where a command supports it). TLS verification is always on; use --ca-file to trust an
extra CA. The tenant always comes from your token, never from a flag.

Exit codes:
   0  success
   1  generic error
   2  vault sealed
   3  not authenticated / insufficient scope (401, 403)
   4  tenant mismatch
   5  rate limited (429)
   6  validation failed (422)
   7  plan compilation failed
   8  safety envelope rejected
   9  cluster unhealthy (503)
  10  DR drill failed
  64  usage error (bad flags or arguments)
  69  command not implemented yet (server contract pending)
  78  configuration error
